@* Theme documentation generated from ThemeTokenCatalog (ADR 0103 §2.3): the file format, where
   themes live, the value types and every token. *@
<article class="theme-docs">
    <section>
        <h3>Theme files</h3>
        <p>
            A theme is a text file ending in <code>.theme</code>. Save it in
            <code>~/.config/hackeros/themes/</code> for yourself; an administrator can copy it to
            <code>/etc/hackeros/themes/</code> for every user. The file is also the export: copy it,
            send it, open it here.
        </p>
<pre class="docs-sample">[theme]
id = neon-crypt
name = Neon Crypt
base = hackeros
platforms = desktop, mobile

[tokens]
--hos-bg-base = #0b0f0b
--hos-accent = #39ff14
--hos-font-mono = "JetBrains Mono", monospace</pre>
        <ul>
            <li><code>id</code>: lowercase letters, digits and dashes; it cannot reuse a built-in theme or a theme of <code>/etc</code>.</li>
            <li><code>base</code>: a built-in theme. A token you do not set keeps the base theme's value.</li>
            <li><code>platforms</code>: <code>desktop</code>, <code>mobile</code> or both. On a form factor the base theme does not style, the tokens apply over that form factor's default theme.</li>
            <li>Only the tokens below are read, and each value is checked against its type. An invalid line is ignored with a warning; there is no free CSS, no remote font or image and no script.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3>Value types</h3>
        <dl class="docs-types">
            <dt>Color</dt><dd><code>#39ff14</code>, <code>#39ff14cc</code>, <code>rgb(57 255 20)</code>, <code>rgb(57 255 20 / 40%)</code>, <code>hsl(110 100% 54%)</code> or a color name such as <code>teal</code>.</dd>
            <dt>Length</dt><dd><code>0</code>, or a number with <code>px</code>, <code>rem</code>, <code>em</code>, <code>%</code>, <code>vh</code> or <code>vw</code>.</dd>
            <dt>Duration</dt><dd><code>150ms</code> or <code>0.2s</code>, optionally followed by <code>ease</code>, <code>linear</code>, <code>ease-in</code>, <code>ease-out</code> or <code>ease-in-out</code>. Ignored when animations are turned off.</dd>
            <dt>FontFamily</dt><dd>Names separated by commas: <code>"Fira Code", monospace</code>. Only fonts installed on the machine are used.</dd>
            <dt>Number</dt><dd>A plain number: <code>600</code>, <code>0.8</code>.</dd>
        </dl>
    </section>

    @foreach (ThemeTokenGroup group in Enum.GetValues<ThemeTokenGroup>())
    {
        <section>
            <h3>@group</h3>
            <table class="docs-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">What it changes</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (ThemeTokenDefinition token in ThemeTokenCatalog.InGroup(group))
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>@token.Name</code><span class="docs-label">@token.Label</span></td>
                            <td>@token.Type</td>
                            <td>
                                @token.Description
                                @if (token.RgbCompanion is { } companion)
                                {
                                    <span class="docs-companion">Also sets <code>@companion</code>.</span>
                                }
                            </td>
                            <td><code>@token.Example</code></td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>
    }
</article>
